  "full_text": "Okay, I'm aspiring to be a modern Commodore 64. This is a secondary operating system. It is not a general purpose. And therefore, we cherry pick our goals in order, we get to pick what it does. I seek incredible power with minimal code. Therefore, I will pick my, what it does. I'm free to pick what it does. I'm picking so that the code is exceptionally minimal. And my definition of what this operating system must do is the 30 games and applications that are already on it. It meets the design goals. Nobody plays two video games at once. Okay? So some idiot is a faggot. He's like... It doesn't play two video games at once. It's not any good. You're a fucking idiot. Fuck you.",
